# Start octo and wait for the OCTO> prompt
# Type [select 1 as a] without pressing Enter, then press Ctrl-C
PASS : Ctrl-C discards the line and displays a new OCTO> prompt
# Run [select 2 as b;]
PASS : Only [select 2 as b;] runs
# Press Ctrl-C twice at an empty OCTO> prompt
PASS : First Ctrl-C at an empty prompt displays a new OCTO> prompt
PASS : Second Ctrl-C at an empty prompt displays a new OCTO> prompt
# Enter [select * from nosuch] (a query on an unknown table) without a semicolon, then press Ctrl-C on the next line
PASS : Ctrl-C after the first line of a query displays a new OCTO> prompt
# Run [select id from names where id = 3;]
PASS : Only [select id from names where id = 3;] runs, with no error for the discarded query
# Enter [select 'abc] (a string that is not terminated), press Ctrl-C, then press Enter on the empty line
PASS : Ctrl-C inside a string that spans lines displays a new OCTO> prompt
# Run [select 5 as e;]
PASS : Only [select 5 as e;] runs
# Enter [select 6] as the first line of a query, press Ctrl-C, then press Ctrl-D
PASS : Ctrl-C after the first line of a query displays a new OCTO> prompt
PASS : Ctrl-D after Ctrl-C terminates octo with exit status 0 and does not run [select 6]
